	Here are some questions I collected while I play NetHack. While 
answering these please bear in mind I've never been below level 9. So, 
please answer in a newbie context. I'm sure I'll come up with more. By 
the way, I know I can look in the source code for these but I'm not 
looking for spoilers. I just wanna learn how some of the things work 
without spoiling much. Thanks all in advance.

	1) When you are bitten by werejackal for example, are you screwed for 
life? Are there things you can do to cure yourself or prevent being 
bitten short of running away or teleporting?
	2) Use of sinks and fountains: Should I drink? Not drink? What are 
benefits and disadvantages? Does it help at all with hunger? What should 
I dip?
	3) Praying: I know it helps with hunger. Though when I prayed a second 
time the god was displeased. Is praying a last resort option? How does 
it work? What does it help with?
	4) Altars: I know it lets you identify cursed/blessed items. Any other 
uses? Obviously type of altar (lawful, etc.) matters. How so?
	5) Being threatened: What does it mean? This happens sometimes when I 
read spellbooks. Also, is it bad to try to read books you cannot easily 
comprehend (game warning)?
	6) Scrolls, spellbooks, potions: The names of these are randomized 
every game. Correct? So I've been just using/reading these to figure out 
what they do every game. Obviously, I end up not using most of them 
because I'm afraid of negative effects. Are there ways of identifying 
these short of scroll of identifications (which needs to be identified 
itself first :) )?
	7) You have some attributes of your character that are displayed when 
you die: You were stealthy, you were a werejackal, you were fast, etc. 
Is there a way to see these during the game? I noticed my monk became 
stealthy (not sure what it does) when he reached level 5 for example. 
So, I guess you gain these attributes though I don't know according to what.
	8) I don't know some of the miscellaneous commands in the game do or 
how/why I should use them. Among these are: #invoke, #offer, #rub, #sit, 
#wipe.
	9) I don't know some of the miscellaneous items in the game do or 
